}
```

### Adding AI (QVAC):

```json
"dependencies": {
  "@qvac/sdk": "^0.11.0",
  "zod": "^4.3.0"
},
"devDependencies": {
  "@qvac/cli": "^0.5.0"
}
```

`@qvac/sdk@0.11` declares `@qvac/cli@^0.4.0` as its peerOptional. The 0.5.x line
is runtime-compatible (no addon-side changes between 0.4 and 0.5 — same deps,
same `bare-pack` floor) but npm strict peer resolution rejects it. Install with
`--legacy-peer-deps` when pinning `^0.5.0`, or pin `^0.4.0` to satisfy the peer
range cleanly:

```bash
# Recommended (latest line, requires the flag once):
npm install -D '@qvac/cli@^0.5.0' --legacy-peer-deps
# Fallback (clean peer resolution, slightly older):
npm install -D '@qvac/cli@^0.4.0'
```

For Expo (mobile) apps additionally pin `react-native-bare-kit` to the exact
version that `@qvac/sdk@0.11` requires:

```json
"dependencies": {
  "react-native-bare-kit": "0.12.3"
}
```
